\ light.8th -- Thinking 8th, Chapter 9
\ Verified with: 8th code/ch09/light.8th
\
\ Store the actual value, not a flag some later code has to check --
\ "light" folds the brightness bit directly into the color itself.
\ n:bor is bitwise-OR on numbers, a different word from the boolean
\ "or" used elsewhere in this chapter -- 8th keeps the two honestly
\ separate, unlike classic Forth where a boolean was just an integer.

0 constant black
1 constant blue
2 constant green

: light  \ color -- color
  8 n:bor ;

blue light . cr    \ => 9

bye
